                <p>See <ref target="#d1350-f4">footnote 4, Document 1350</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1361-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1361-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1361-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1361-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d1359-f1">footnote 1, Document 1359</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1361-f4" n="4" xml:id="d1361-f4-content">
                <p>Ambassador Caffery responded to this final paragraph of telegram 382 on Sept. 9
                    in telegram 318, not printed. Caffery stressed that Egypt needed aid in the form
                    of grants, not loans, and concluded with the thought that American loan
                    assistance would not be regarded as real aid by the Egyptians. (774.5
                    MSP/9–954)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
